  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 114 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThe extended upper pattern remains zonal, meaning systems will be\ntraveling mainly west to east. The lack of amplification of the\npattern prevents any cold air from Canada from making into West\nTexas and eastern New Mexico. In addition, westerly flow will \nkeep moisture to our east eliminating most rain chances. A weak \ncold front arrives Thursday which could bring some isolated to \nscattered showers and storms to the Big Bend, but overall the \nforecast will be dry. Temperatures will also be seasonal with \nhighs in the 60s and 70s.\n\nHennig",
